; ============================================================
; THE BYZANTINE SHADOW
; MODULE 08 EXTENSION -- TRANSACTION REQUIREMENT
; ============================================================
;
; This file is part of Module 08's requirement authority.
; It closes the requirement -> capital boundary for the first
; vertical production slice without hard-coding the Spearman price.
;
; ENGINE AUTHORITY
; ----------------
; The engine defines the current cost of spearman-line through
; up-add-object-cost. The resulting four-resource vector is stored
; in AEGIS-TRANSACTION-FOOD..STONE.
;
; Cost-vector order is:
;   food, wood, stone, gold
;
; AEGIS-TRANSACTION-FOOD = 475
; AEGIS-TRANSACTION-WOOD = 476
; AEGIS-TRANSACTION-GOLD = 477
; AEGIS-TRANSACTION-STONE = 478
;
; These are extended goals and therefore also form a valid UP
; cost-data block. No literal resource price appears below.
;
; This module does NOT:
;   - determine capital feasibility;
;   - modify escrow;
;   - grant authority;
;   - train the unit;
;   - verify completion.
;
; ============================================================
; SPEARMAN TRANSACTION COST
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION AEGIS-TRANSACTION-RESERVING)
    (goal AEGIS-REQUIREMENT AEGIS-REQUIREMENT-SPEARMAN)
=>
    ; Reset the transaction cost vector, then ask the engine for the
    ; cost of exactly one Spearman-line object.
    (up-setup-cost-data 1 AEGIS-TRANSACTION-FOOD)
    (up-add-object-cost c: spearman-line c: 1)
)

; ============================================================
; REQUIREMENT READY
; ============================================================
;
; The requirement is ready only after the transaction cost block has
; been materialized. The rule does not assert the numeric cost.
;
(defrule
    (goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION AEGIS-TRANSACTION-RESERVING)
    (goal AEGIS-REQUIREMENT AEGIS-REQUIREMENT-SPEARMAN)
    (up-compare-goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION-FOOD >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION-WOOD >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION-GOLD >= 0)
    (up-compare-goal AEGIS-TRANSACTION-STONE >= 0)
=>
    (set-goal AEGIS-REQUIREMENT  AEGIS-REQUIREMENT-SPEARMAN)
)

; ============================================================
; INVARIANT
; ============================================================
;
; If the engine changes the Spearman cost, the vector changes with it.
; The capital module must consume this vector rather than a copied
; 60F/40W assumption.
